# An untyped `null` with nothing to give it a type, including a function whose result would be `null`.
mode: check
schema: 'orders.csv'(orderId: string, customerId: string, amount: real, qty: long, small: int, timestamp: datetime, wait: timespan, shipped: bool)
---- query
let x = null;
let y = abs(null);
let z = iff(true, null, null);
let w = null + null;
---- expected
error[DS2009]: cannot tell what type this `null` has
  --> query:1:9
  |
1 | let x = null;
  |         ^^^^ nothing here gives this `null` a type
  |
  = help: write a typed null instead, such as `long(null)`, `string(null)` or `datetime(null)`

